## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses planning, risk management, data integrity, and cross-team governance for a major migration; tests ability to define milestones, ownership, and metrics beyond high-level talk.

## Key Concepts

- Migration strategy and data integrity checks
- Downtime avoidance and phased rollout (canaries, dual-write)
- Rollback criteria, SLAs, and incident readiness
- Cross-team governance and staffing plans
- Metrics dashboards and validation artifacts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Basic idempotent migration hook (illustrative)
async function migrateBatch(batch) {
  for (const record of batch) {
    try {
      await writeToNewPlatform(record);
      await markAsMigrated(record.id);
    } catch (error) {
      await logMigrationError(record.id, error);
      // Continue processing other records
    }
  }
}
```

